{
  "schema_version": 5,
  "type": "bugfix",
  "problem": [
    {
      "text": "The two dependency declarations disagreed: setup.py specified older Torch and unbounded NumPy, omitted several requirements.txt dependencies, and retained a different package set.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_a0d4c0e650284540b4c187816b1ec69c", "call_98a23a98d37c4ae8af69c8675f0350da"]
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": [
    {
      "text": "The change aligns package metadata with requirements.txt while adding safetensors and ninja to the latter and removing tabulate.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_1f7933083ef047a9aec5d43a9c204d96", "call_bd2830ecdd734e55bb07925f194434ee"]
    }
  ],
  "impact": [
    {
      "text": "A standard-library check applying the inspected dependency edits found identical sets of eight declarations in the two installation interfaces.",
      "basis": "execution",
      "evidence": ["call_44ad4f762ba041478fa2335520414d67"]
    }
  ],
  "source_notes": [
    {
      "text": "The parent entry describes a separate fix to native source-path representation; this change instead updates dependency declarations.",
      "basis": "ancestor",
      "evidence": ["call_20d09af0d4fb4dcaabf3ac0e19dfea91"]
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The check models the dependency edits; it does not run setuptools, pip resolution, native compilation, or application tests.",
    "The inspected evidence does not establish why each minimum version is necessary or whether the resulting dependencies suffice for every optional workflow."
  ],
  "links": ["d43424e20171a6de5eed75dee0eb263b397e8c48"],
  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "packaging",
      "title": "Consistent installation dependencies",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "setup.py passes install_requires directly to setuptools.setup. Its replacement list requires torch>=2.6.0, flash_attn>=2.7.4.post1, tokenizers>=0.21.1, numpy>=2.1.0, rich, typing_extensions, ninja and safetensors>=0.3.2. The version numbers are lower bounds rather than exact pins.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_98a23a98d37c4ae8af69c8675f0350da", "call_bd2830ecdd734e55bb07925f194434ee"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Package metadata drops pandas, fastparquet, sentencepiece, pygments, websockets, regex and pillow. Ninja, safetensors and rich remain; Torch's lower bound rises from 2.2.0 to 2.6.0 and NumPy gains the 2.1.0 bound already present in requirements.txt.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_bd2830ecdd734e55bb07925f194434ee", "call_a0d4c0e650284540b4c187816b1ec69c"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Alignment removes a dependency-set difference between the two installation routes, but the lists remain independently maintained, so future edits can diverge again.",
          "basis": "inference",
          "evidence": ["call_1f7933083ef047a9aec5d43a9c204d96", "call_bd2830ecdd734e55bb07925f194434ee"]
        },
        {
          "text": "This is not a build-bootstrap redesign: setup.py still checks whether Torch is already available before configuring CUDAExtension and BuildExtension, and EXLLAMA_NOCOMPILE still disables precompilation.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_98a23a98d37c4ae8af69c8675f0350da", "call_bd2830ecdd734e55bb07925f194434ee"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": [],
  "summary": "Aligns setup.py and requirements.txt on eight dependencies, updates minimum versions, and removes divergent declarations."
}
